  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: 3 days of watery diarrhea requiring frequent toilet use.\n- Symptoms (onset/duration/severity/agg/alg): Started ~3 days ago. Loose, watery stools 6–7 times/day. Crampy, intermittent lower abdominal pain localized to the left side. Vomiting at onset but has stopped. Felt feverish at symptom onset (patient-noted temperature), currently afebrile. Weakness/shakiness and reduced appetite. Able to tolerate fluids (soups, smoothies). Symptoms impairing daily activities and work.\n- Past medical history: Asthma (uses an inhaler; reportedly controlled).\n- Medications / allergies: Inhaler only. No other medications reported. No allergies mentioned.\n- Family / social history: Lives with wife and two children. One child had vomiting (did not have diarrhea). Works as an accountant. Non-smoker. Does not drink alcohol.\n- Vital signs / exam findings: No measured vitals documented. No physical exam findings recorded; clinician planned conservative management and did not perform/r eport exam/vitals.\n- Labs / imaging: None mentioned; no stool studies done yet.\n- Exposure history: Ate a Chinese takeaway ~4 days ago. No other known sick contacts except one child who vomited.\n- Other relevant: No blood in stool or vomit. No ongoing fever reported at visit. Has been continuing to attend work despite symptoms.",
